# laurus SUSFS perf fragment: trim debug/tracing overhead.
# KSU/SUSFS, KALLSYMS_ALL, module signing and SELinux are untouched; the boot image
# (not this fragment) decides permissive vs enforcing.
#
# Not disablable here:
#   FRAME_POINTER  — arm64 4.14 selects it in arch/arm64/Kconfig.
#   DEBUG_LIST     — selected by CONFIG_BUG_ON_DATA_CORRUPTION (hardening), kept on purpose.
# Optional max-perf (not enabled): CONFIG_INIT_ON_ALLOC_DEFAULT_ON=n, BUG_ON_DATA_CORRUPTION=n.
# FTRACE stays on: CONFIG_BPF_EVENTS depends on it, and Android's libmeminfo aborts
# in BpfMapRO::abortOnMismatch (system_server crash loop) without the GPU-mem BPF maps.
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO is not set
# CONFIG_SCHED_DEBUG is not set
# CONFIG_SCHEDSTATS is not set
